{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1557847-my-scion-campaign","id":1557847,"title":"My Scion Campaign","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-01-22T20:30:05-08:00","id":1557847,"title":"My Scion Campaign","content":"I'm the storyteller for a Scion Campaign that has been running for about 5 years now. We don't play weekly, I'd say, we have about 12-14 sessions a year. We are all very busy, but we are all committed to the game and we make it work.<br /> <br /> I have been playing with this gaming group, which includes my wife and long time friends since about 1995. Over the years, this gaming group has played (in order of play) three Changeling the Dreaming campaigns, two Changeling the Lost campaigns and one Mummy the Curse campaign. Scion is now our &quot;go to&quot; game.<br /> <br /> We recently played our first session of the new year. That session was the beginning of the Demigod phase of our campaign. We started the session by visiting the Secret Library, profiled in the Realms of Magic and Mystery book.<br /> <br /> Starting with our next session, I hope to post session updates of the Scion games, so people can see what we are doing with Scion. Let me know if you have any questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Organizer for the Dead Gamers Society: The So Cal World of Darkness Meetup. </span><a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/</a>","edited":{"userid":85,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/85-drumheller","user":"Drumheller","date":". 01-22-2026, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/85-drumheller","name":"Drumheller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar85_2.jpeg","title":"Member